2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115181 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48438bb9-4a21-5d55-96f0-948c0c989fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254285} {:answer/id #uuid "66fa35a2-e7a7-5e1e-9818-392b0299bc78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254600} {:answer/id #uuid "82cacc30-33e9-5893-99d3-5ef580e7284b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254831} {:answer/id #uuid "caba6445-ae90-5115-93c6-ab627020faa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255473} {:answer/id #uuid "cd649532-af80-594b-92df-39158e97f458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caba6445-ae90-5115-93c6-ab627020faa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255473} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3e3129-2c3b-5749-96a9-d8234f09b53a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e821a2c-70b6-5ded-9b65-8ac018a20911" :question/math-academy-id "q-120487" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}?$\n\n- $4\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7=3+2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+3=1$ $$\n- $2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-5=-6$" :question/worked-solution "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=5$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-2$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ea0f9e5-6ff5-59fe-9529-c971786bf12f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255067} {:answer/id #uuid "a17ade41-98aa-506c-9ec8-1af48400efa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255091} {:answer/id #uuid "ccec92a2-4176-5f0e-98b9-9281024e3dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255491} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2b7028-aa27-5a01-beb8-3f8ffb9bd8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255743} {:answer/id #uuid "f87c9d22-4ab8-5daf-8288-8a1a9b1698c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.ty